# The capture build for resources/graphics/MatrixTime5.png, and nothing else (#128).
#
# Layered over monkey.jungle rather than replacing it, so every shared setting --
# the generated launcher icon mapping, sourcePath, the type check level -- comes
# from the one file that defines them, and the manifest from the edition jungle:
#
#   monkeyc -f "monkey.jungle;graphics.jungle;lite.jungle" ...
#
# monkeyc -f takes a semicolon-separated list and later files override earlier ones,
# so this reassignment replaces monkey.jungle's exclusion rather than adding to it.
# That is also why the edition jungle comes AFTER this one, never before it (#135):
# lite.jungle appends (:premium) to whatever list it finds, and a replacement made
# after it would drop that exclusion without a word. tools/make-graphics.py passes
# all three files for the always-on frame; the four woken frames are captured from
# monkey.jungle and lite.jungle alone.
#
# The effect is to compile View.inLowPower's forced definition, which makes onUpdate
# take the drawLowPower branch on every frame. See the comment in source/View.mc for
# why a forced frame is a truthful always-on frame, and monkey.jungle for the gate.
base.excludeAnnotations = realLowPower
